tention, stress resilience, responsibility are crucial. C's communication difficulty may be a bigger safety risk than D's moody/loner? Both are concerning. But D's \"arrogant\" and \"weak leadership\" may be more severe for crew cooperation. C's egocentric may also be severe. However C's \"puts concern for others above everything\" suggests some crew orientation. So perhaps C is better overall despite communication issues, if we can train. But we need to decide.\n\nGiven the panel hasn't fully discussed A and D, but we have now some info. I think we can argue that Candidate C remains the leading candidate because of quick correct decisions, excellent attention, concern for others, and calmness (implied). The concerns about communication and egocentric attitude are notable but may be mitigated with training, whereas D's arrogance and weak leadership are more fundamental for crew cooperation. So I will vote for Candidate C.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Agent 2's focus on C, but I will add that D's arrogance and weak leadership raise crew cooperation concerns, making C still preferable despite communication issues. Provide evidence.\n\nProceed."}
